            <div class="imagemeta col-md-4">
                <h3>Dial it in</h3>
                <p>Coming from an illustration background, I'm always happy to dive into visual design. My goal is to create beautiful, intuitive and accessible interfaces that meet users with an understanding of the job they're there to do, and information organized in a way that helps them find what they're looking for.</p> 
                <p>Over the years, I've had the honor of having my UI work featured in Apple's TV commercials and iPhone sales kiosks and placed in the hands of every Starbucks barista <em>and</em> every Google developer.</p>
            </div>
  
            <div class="images col-md-3">
                <img class="image" src="/images/process/p2t_ipad.png" />
            </div>

        </div>   
    </div>
</section>
 


<section class="projectsection">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
  

            <div class="imagemeta col-md-6">
                <h3>Operationalize, democratize</h3>
     
            <p>As a product moves from idea to production to iteration, design and project docs, component libraries and codebases grow into <strong>resources for both internal and external teams.</strong></p>
            
            <p>I've worked extensively <strong>building on existing design systems</strong> at large companies with mature design practices. When those practices don't yet exist, my system for self-documenting Figma files (based heavily on Git's system of branches and commits) helps new hires onbaord quickly and preserves work in the case of rotating contractors. My system for specs has been invaluable in facilitating conversations with dev, compliance and QA and component libraries preserve work for whoever's bulding what comes next.</p> 

            </div>

            <div class="images col-md-6">
                <img class="image" src="/images/process/operationalize2.png" />
            </div>

        </div>   
    </div>
</section>

<section class="projectsection dark">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
  
            <div class="images col-md-8">
                <img class="image" src="/images/process/publish.png" />
            </div>

            <div class="imagemeta col-md-4">
                <h3>Publish or perish</h3>
                <p>Through every project, I document work in a combination of team notebook with interview and research notes, a project board for stakeholders, and series of shorter-form presentations and summaries to share with leadership.</p>
        
            <p>These docs have proven themselves to be valuable tools for winning hearts and minds within the organization, and I've often been asked to share them with other teams, VPs and the C-suite for the value they communicate about our team's work. Since adopting this practice, my teams have expressed having a much <strong>easier time finding resources for our projects,</strong> and an <strong>increase in positive feedback from leadership.</strong></p>
      
            </div>

        </div>   
    </div>
</section>